{
  "id": "Compound::DB00921 - Gene::1565",
  "verbalization": "Buprenorphine exhibits a strong binding interaction with Cyp2c8 and Cyp3a7, which are both involved in the metabolism of arachidonic acid. This binding leads to the participation of these enzymes in the epoxygenation and monooxygenation of arachidonic acid, respectively. These enzymatic activities ultimately contribute to the participation of Cyp2d6 in the metabolic pathway of arachidonic acid. The shared involvement of Cyp2d6 in the metabolism of arachidonic acid suggests a potential mechanistic link between Buprenorphine and Cyp2d6, mediated through the arachidonic acid metabolic pathway. The evidence from the three paths is consistent, with similar scores indicating a robust relationship, and the overlapping roles of Cyp2d6 in the metabolism of arachidonic acid provide a plausible mechanism for the observed interaction. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Cyp2d6 in the metabolic processing of arachidonic acid, which is a key step in the production of pro-inflammatory mediators. This suggests that Buprenorphine may influence Cyp2d6 through the arachidonic acid metabolic pathway, potentially affecting the metabolism of arachidonic acid and its downstream effects.",
